I arrive at a large square.
There are many people.
But I do not see the water.
I am looking for the harbour.
I see an older man on the pavement.
I stop him.
"Excuse me," I say.
"Where is the harbour?"
The older man nods.
He points ahead.
"Walk straight across the square," he says.
"Go past the museum."
"And turn right."
I look across the square.
I see a large building.
It is the museum.
"Thank you very much," I say.
"You are welcome," he replies.
I continue walking.
